Mara: Please, before you say anything. We're not sick. Nobody's been bitten. We walked from the coast.
Mara: My father can't walk much further, and Ilse hasn't slept in two days. The officer says the town will decide.
- You'll stay. I'll tell Ruth myself.
	Mara: You'd do that? For people you don't know?
	Mara: Thank you. I won't forget it. None of us will.
	[signal arg="flag:refugees_vouched"]
- It's not my call. The town will decide.
	Mara: That's fair. It's more than most places gave us.
	[signal arg="flag:refugees_heard"]
- What happened on the coast?
	Mara: The quiet came first. Then the boats stopped coming in. Then the people who went to see didn't come back.
	Mara: We left the night the lighthouse went dark.
